			<div class="content" id="post-content-1777353">
									

<p>Okay, I explained my reasons for disliking this in PM when I was looking over the draft, and since nothing has changed, I'll just paste it here.</p>
<p>Hmm<br />
First of all, why is this Keter? I mean, sure, it somehow broke out of a steel block, but given there's no detail given, it just feels like something for it to do that'd make it Keter. I mean… even with technology it takes a little time to start fucking up . . it almost feels like you could set it up in a way that propelled chunks would just fall back in - you know, fit a sheet metal cone around the entrance , like those injured cat / dog collars.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Agents with experience using antique and ancient weaponry are to be preferred.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I dislike this as well. I mean, why don't you specify what they have to be proficient with, and if you need it . .. the Foundation can train the people it needs.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>From outside the active radius, changes can be observed in clothing, speech, and behavior of persons inside the anomaly. Additionally, technology, building materials and machines will first regress to simpler forms before disappearing completely once temporal displacement becomes sufficient to preclude the object's existence. SCP-XXXX will also change appearance as the event progresses2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, well. I can't say I'm a huge fan of the effect, and it sort of comes out from the blue.<br />
Also, what with personnel reverting. I mean, if they revert to a time before this was contained, they wouldn't know the containment procedures, would they?</p>
<p>And then you have the shit-covered clippings that exploit the fact. . wait.<br />
What about waxed cloth? That sort of &quot;hazmat&quot; protection would likely prevent contact with the shit, yet was available for ages!</p>
<p>I dunno. This one kinda does little for me overall.</p>

